From 871e4d8b32c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Srinivas Kandagatla <srinivas.kandagatla@linaro.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Sep 2022 13:42:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: update status from device id 1

QCom SoundWire auto-enumeration reserves device ID 0. Do not pass the
reserved status slot to the SoundWire core. The TCL ACPI kernel currently
starts this loop at zero, which leaves the status array misaligned with the
slave device IDs and can make raw SWRM_MCP_SLV_STATUS disagree with sysfs.

This context is adapted to the TCL 7.2.4 branch, whose loop uses '<' and
has no slave_status assignment.

Upstream fix: 8039b6f3e5c7 (soundwire: qcom: update status from device id 1)

Signed-off-by: Srinivas Kandagatla <srinivas.kandagatla@linaro.org>
---
 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -232,8 +232,8 @@ static void qcom_swrm_get_device_status(struct qcom_swrm_ctrl *ctrl)
 	ctrl->reg_read(ctrl, SWRM_MCP_SLV_STATUS, &val);
 
-	for (i = 0; i < SDW_MAX_DEVICES; i++) {
+	for (i = 1; i < SDW_MAX_DEVICES; i++) {
 		u32 s;
 
 		s = (val >> (i * 2));
 		s &= SWRM_MCP_SLV_STATUS_MASK;
 		ctrl->status[i] = s;
-- 
2.39.0
